description:
Design a checksum calculator that takes an n-bit wide input data vector and computes its checksum, producing an m-bit wide output. The module sums the values of the input data words and then computes the final checksum by taking the sum modulo \( 2^m \). The parameters n and m can be configured to define the bit width of the input data and the size of the checksum, respectively.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] data,
  output [m-1:0] chksum
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] data,
  output [m-1:0] chksum
);parameter n = 8; // number of data words
parameter m = 16; // number of bits in each data word

reg [m-1:0] sum; // register to hold the sum of the data words
integer i; // Declare the loop variable

// compute the sum of the data words
always @ (data) begin
  sum = 0;
  for (i = 0; i < n; i = i + 1) begin
    sum = sum + data[i];
  end
end

// compute the checksum by taking the sum modulo 2^m
assign chksum = sum % (1 << m);

endmodule

