description:
Implement the Verilog module based on the following description.
Build a 128-bit shift register with synchronous load and clear. The shifter can shift left or right by 1 or 16 bit positions, selected by "amount."

// Signals are defined as below:
// (1) load: Loads shift register with data[127:0] instead of shifting. Active high.
// (2) ena: Chooses whether to shift. Active high. 
// (3) clr: Clears the register to 0. Active high.
// (4) amount: Chooses which direction and how much to shift. 
//     (a) 2'b00: shift left by 1 bit. 
//     (b) 2'b01: shift left by 16 bits. 
//     (c) 2'b10: shift right by 1 bit. 
//     (d) 2'b11: shift right by 16 bits. 
// (5) q: The contents of the shifter.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input load,
    input ena,
    input clr,
    input [1:0] amount,
    input [127:0] data,
    output reg [127:0] q);

