Design a bidirectional I/O pad with output enable control. The module interfaces with external signals, using a tristate buffer to control the data flow to and from the pad. When the output enable (oe) is high, the module drives the pad with the data input; otherwise, it places the pad in high impedance mode. The incoming signal from the pad is assigned to the output (out), facilitating both transmission and reception of signals while allowing for impedance control through external reference voltages.
