description:
Design a binary counter with a parameterizable width, N. The counter increments its value by the input 'cin' on each rising edge of the clock 'clk', provided that the reset signal is not asserted, which would set the counter to zero. An additional output 'cout' indicates a carry condition, which is high when all bits of the counter are set and 'cin' is also high. This module effectively combines the functionality of a synchronous counter with a carry output for cascading connections in larger digital designs.
module top_module(
    q,cout,reset, cin, clk
);

code:
module top_module(
    q,cout,reset, cin, clk
);parameter N = 4;
    output reg [N:1]q;
    output cout;
    input reset, cin, clk;
    always @(posedge clk) 
    begin
        q <= reset ? 0 : q + cin;
    end
    assign cout = &q && cin;endmodule

