description:
Design a 32-bit multiplier block that computes a specific multiplication operation on a 32-bit input signal. The block performs several left shifts and arithmetic operations on the input data to derive the output. Specifically, it employs shifts and subtractions to manipulate the input data to produce a resultant value, which is then assigned to the output. This design effectively implements a custom multiplication algorithm that leverages bitwise operations and arithmetic to achieve the final output.
